    "caption": "Grafana keeps dashboards and settings in its own database and proxies every query to the data sources, which hold the actual telemetry.",
    "alt": "A browser loads the Grafana frontend and asks the Grafana backend for dashboards and query results. The backend reads dashboards, users and alert rules from its database, MySQL or Postgres in production. For each panel the backend's data source plugins query Prometheus for metrics, Loki for logs and Tempo for traces. Provisioning files or Git Sync write dashboards and data sources into Grafana from version control.",
